{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:35:21Z","created_by_operation":"op_df889bacf4cc48f6a526752b2e076f63","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_08718dcc1fef5a641dca9dda41c0404fbe8391f1f35a2f5867e70d534f375033","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=components","setting":"rath-team/openrath@82819467b001 snapshot 5bcf2c869c8a34af","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_2145ab3a99a1ff6bc49e5f879e235c78111c56075f1a4236fac868a55ba17468","slc_61746d896dc890c7d27c3ba7b3e62491f2f2a95f12c3ab54de716049cf7648aa"],"source_ids":["src_4347e70250ca59d3a74f138eeee67b26"],"text":"OpenRath exposes core runtime objects: Session (conversation state and inter-agent lineage), Sandbox (tool execution placement), Memory, Tool, Agent, Workflow, and Selector.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:35:21Z","updated_by_operation":"op_df889bacf4cc48f6a526752b2e076f63"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:35:21Z","created_by_operation":"op_df889bacf4cc48f6a526752b2e076f63","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_112583f5488ba75ac71dfdff75a6004fbb69b0176ae060e156d58c592f860d16","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=design-choices","setting":"rath-team/openrath@82819467b001 snapshot 5bcf2c869c8a34af","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_1db2c3cc968689bdb300cc8a44f77a074ba0b5d0b255485241dd747ebbf48e8b","slc_ab65f64fd9a7ad29d43e7320c634456162bb9fb170977e6a7d347887aed4504c"],"source_ids":["src_4347e70250ca59d3a74f138eeee67b26"],"text":"OpenRath is Session-first rather than agent-loop-first, so multi-agent, multi-branch, durable-memory, sandboxed, and lineage-traced workloads share one flowing value.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:35:21Z","updated_by_operation":"op_df889bacf4cc48f6a526752b2e076f63"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:35:21Z","created_by_operation":"op_df889bacf4cc48f6a526752b2e076f63","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_1852125020a00c78d41062e27ac626a7968f037f65ea2b915751bc1190436146","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=interfaces","setting":"rath-team/openrath@82819467b001 snapshot 5bcf2c869c8a34af","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_37bcb37a1f7adc968b42a8ceac016c6dc586e75c552debbdb72be59bcae7247f","slc_dc861cb3fa338ea31486c1ad83cdcfa35a6cbc40d70f18b7ac105ce4ded4211f","slc_f1ba0700c4a8d7e7c407b03b6e00ade4c9647e8bfd080902d07e2e7b6f243d8d"],"source_ids":["src_4347e70250ca59d3a74f138eeee67b26"],"text":"flow.Workflow subclasses implement forward(session) -> Session, enabling nesting of agents, forks, compression, tools, and child workflows without a new state format per layer.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:35:21Z","updated_by_operation":"op_df889bacf4cc48f6a526752b2e076f63"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:35:21Z","created_by_operation":"op_df889bacf4cc48f6a526752b2e076f63","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_2a950178b278ee9d18014302a270ca3c6d4b51880d7d4a6088e9066b3efd07f7","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=dependencies","setting":"rath-team/openrath@82819467b001 snapshot 5bcf2c869c8a34af","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_687f20e0d1de64c1493d5920759d7db0375a34147fa85f47f0532d0dc7d98acf","slc_bfc87d6c805eccfaabd345378e88237943e422293caeae4505ff6d753d4c3867"],"source_ids":["src_4347e70250ca59d3a74f138eeee67b26"],"text":"The production data plane uses PostgreSQL as source of truth, Redis for signaling acceleration, and S3-compatible artifact storage; the server/postgres extra installs via pip with openrath-migrate for schema migration.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:35:21Z","updated_by_operation":"op_df889bacf4cc48f6a526752b2e076f63"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:35:21Z","created_by_operation":"op_df889bacf4cc48f6a526752b2e076f63","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_3026dac26635880504341eefcd0002bf4313ac5a9108b68e5c4a278a5c5dc412","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=limitations","setting":"rath-team/openrath@82819467b001 snapshot 5bcf2c869c8a34af","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_7fa4898994f2c7ddaefacbb1791ebe2f583755231a5f58cfe698ff45cdff43fa"],"source_ids":["src_4347e70250ca59d3a74f138eeee67b26"],"text":"The Agent Server HTTP surface is explicitly labeled Beta, and v1 JSONL imports are historical records rather than resumable active Runs.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:35:21Z","updated_by_operation":"op_df889bacf4cc48f6a526752b2e076f63"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:35:21Z","created_by_operation":"op_df889bacf4cc48f6a526752b2e076f63","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_31844418c3a3884a082d24b4c0f1d764099194d7490a33c3b4e96ca73ef41422","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=memory-state","setting":"rath-team/openrath@82819467b001 snapshot 5bcf2c869c8a34af","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_0a88e569228fd1c57ca9f7d2c868928a109bb9ad7462b93d18a74a4e3d553157"],"source_ids":["src_4347e70250ca59d3a74f138eeee67b26"],"text":"The base install ships a zero-dependency local memory backend storing data under .openrath/memory/ with lexical BM25 recall, optional embeddings, and OpenViking as an optional external backend.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:35:21Z","updated_by_operation":"op_df889bacf4cc48f6a526752b2e076f63"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:35:21Z","created_by_operation":"op_df889bacf4cc48f6a526752b2e076f63","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_3e95c12ebf221e044c86c9e88c869045b330a658c505877b799cb53e830883f1","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=components","setting":"rath-team/openrath@82819467b001 snapshot 5bcf2c869c8a34af","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_687f20e0d1de64c1493d5920759d7db0375a34147fa85f47f0532d0dc7d98acf","slc_fe35cfa723ed4eabdf6da28f4777be7a45e18ae6fb9bcb83781e37299ef6d728"],"source_ids":["src_4347e70250ca59d3a74f138eeee67b26"],"text":"v2.0.0 adds a durable production layer: @step/@router boundaries compile to immutable plans; Runs, Events, and Checkpoints survive process and worker restarts, with leases, fencing, retries, and resumable queues.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:35:21Z","updated_by_operation":"op_df889bacf4cc48f6a526752b2e076f63"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:35:21Z","created_by_operation":"op_df889bacf4cc48f6a526752b2e076f63","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_49417797f1e066ab07af0988d4b1eae418d4468cad7a05388f58a570e0a198b4","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=orchestration","setting":"rath-team/openrath@82819467b001 snapshot 5bcf2c869c8a34af","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_15848e1fd25cc37fa4b96fbd92a65daa2983818b1298843ff62f24d9ef6798e4","slc_4943fc941acad46c843723da6d2cccbe98f39b1249046d66effb8702e63e6bd2"],"source_ids":["src_4347e70250ca59d3a74f138eeee67b26"],"text":"flow.Selector is an LLM-backed router over self-describing workflows that returns the next workflow or a no-op EmptyWorkflow, keeping if/while control flow in plain Python.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:35:21Z","updated_by_operation":"op_df889bacf4cc48f6a526752b2e076f63"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:35:21Z","created_by_operation":"op_df889bacf4cc48f6a526752b2e076f63","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_4c98292f853f8b96fc40a1eab42ed11bdd2a74a143a3e6475b35b8c1c0bb50be","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=interfaces","setting":"rath-team/openrath@82819467b001 snapshot 5bcf2c869c8a34af","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_0d18e61fb7ea7f5cfe7ea20640216cbf5b2cef7d7e5298b536992ba8c86cfc3d","slc_f86b0ccba2f2292ef09d87de8e81f87e70b55976f8df6cff7af53262c6f9d887"],"source_ids":["src_4347e70250ca59d3a74f138eeee67b26"],"text":"FlowToolCall is the model-visible tool abstraction combining name, description, JSON schema, and a Python call over a Session; BackendTool* is the lower-level payload consumed by sandbox backends.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:35:21Z","updated_by_operation":"op_df889bacf4cc48f6a526752b2e076f63"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:35:21Z","created_by_operation":"op_df889bacf4cc48f6a526752b2e076f63","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_a7ce7641325d7e898a88e7ce3727c8d0058aead33d66d77ac684ce34d486ef6a","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=design-choices","setting":"rath-team/openrath@82819467b001 snapshot 5bcf2c869c8a34af","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_1b5b8e206b9a7d0e9357dadd0c73d0165e4538135969b9614140dd12e434d15e"],"source_ids":["src_4347e70250ca59d3a74f138eeee67b26"],"text":"The framework maps PyTorch concepts to agent concepts: Session as Tensor, Sandbox/Backend as Device, Memory as Parameter, Tool as Function, Agent as nn.Linear, Workflow as nn.Module, Selector as control flow.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:35:21Z","updated_by_operation":"op_df889bacf4cc48f6a526752b2e076f63"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:35:21Z","created_by_operation":"op_df889bacf4cc48f6a526752b2e076f63","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_aa38937715b490a22fcdeaf2587b1bd5715f19976b50cb48cf360a275894066c","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=interfaces","setting":"rath-team/openrath@82819467b001 snapshot 5bcf2c869c8a34af","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_5095cf5fd347c0ca54735d3327eab194e35ff902c45932cf32b74dfcf7f7e186"],"source_ids":["src_4347e70250ca59d3a74f138eeee67b26"],"text":"The local sandbox backend is always available and runs file, command, and code tools against the host workspace; an optional opensandbox backend connects the same tool layer to a containerized runtime, and sessions retain sandbox ownership across tool calls.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:35:21Z","updated_by_operation":"op_df889bacf4cc48f6a526752b2e076f63"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:35:21Z","created_by_operation":"op_df889bacf4cc48f6a526752b2e076f63","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_bc51bb8c513d4cb9cf1120639ce7323b7cf3d265a68b8d419d4de3e721849bf6","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=tools-permissions","setting":"rath-team/openrath@82819467b001 snapshot 5bcf2c869c8a34af","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_049eefc979591987510d0eb54f106e53ef78caf96b4587d30d5492aaf8445984","slc_687f20e0d1de64c1493d5920759d7db0375a34147fa85f47f0532d0dc7d98acf"],"source_ids":["src_4347e70250ca59d3a74f138eeee67b26"],"text":"Agent Server tokens carry explicit action grants, object access is tenant/project scoped, runtime identities need no DDL privileges, and an Effect Ledger stops ambiguous non-idempotent effects in NEEDS_REVIEW rather than replaying them.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:35:21Z","updated_by_operation":"op_df889bacf4cc48f6a526752b2e076f63"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:35:21Z","created_by_operation":"op_df889bacf4cc48f6a526752b2e076f63","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_d01fec61cdeb3004392391a2f7f7613a4271fecb15a19289a9f7d4b885aeabcc","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=interfaces","setting":"rath-team/openrath@82819467b001 snapshot 5bcf2c869c8a34af","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_66684fa69109e40ae3ecf2b1a370794861f00337629e7f60e4f1113e79e9d002","slc_b8ce462b80f490782c41f926ae025c86c7c78af1d7c418f41787f1be4ea4463d"],"source_ids":["src_4347e70250ca59d3a74f138eeee67b26"],"text":"Session supports fork(), detach(), merge(...), JSONL serialization, sandbox binding via session.to(\"local\", spec=\"./\"), plus from_user_message and from_agent_prompt constructors.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:35:21Z","updated_by_operation":"op_df889bacf4cc48f6a526752b2e076f63"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:35:21Z","created_by_operation":"op_df889bacf4cc48f6a526752b2e076f63","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_e6db68cdcf5b34a58d1f53f3a04071a9c48a45f1162deccfc420c66a24a997b0","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=memory-state","setting":"rath-team/openrath@82819467b001 snapshot 5bcf2c869c8a34af","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_123618e4dbf374ca3348e0b5bde0778d1b291315379193f342e2df6a9b9607bb"],"source_ids":["src_4347e70250ca59d3a74f138eeee67b26"],"text":"Agent memory APIs include memory= binding at construction, remember_memory, recall_memory, commit_memory, and commit_on_forward=True for automatic commits.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:35:21Z","updated_by_operation":"op_df889bacf4cc48f6a526752b2e076f63"}
